From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 10/14] Plutonium: the Plutonium DevTools domain, and DevTools
 on a Unix socket

The browser target's Plutonium domain (cros_protocol.pdl) for the helper and its agents: windows, tabs, input, notifications, media, the hardware keys. DevTools are served on a Unix socket that only this user's processes may connect to (--plutonium-remote-debugging-socket).

It holds these changes:
- agents drive windows and tabs over DevTools
- the hardware keys go to the helper's desktop services; the browser's media session in the Plutonium domain
- tabs' web notifications and the host's color scheme in the Plutonium domain
- DevTools Plutonium.setWindowOriginTag
- DevTools on a Unix socket for this user only (--plutonium-remote-debugging-socket)

and the parts in these files of:
- Chrome's own UI in the shell (DevTools, context menus, keys)
- agent keyboard focus beside the user's; the compositor decorates every window
- common plumbing for tab features
- downloads for the shells' tabs
- incognito tabs, each in a throwaway off-the-record profile
- screen capture for shells, capture requests to the focused shell
- several displays, a shell per display, one window in one place
- an agent sees and uses a window's popups
- the lock screen and idle: Ash's own lock over every display, Super+L, the idle time, the wake locks and the displays' power in the Plutonium domain
- agents type through the session's keymap, and a temporary one for what it lacks
- ext_idle_notify_v1, apps hear when the user is idle
- desktop settings and a display configuration tool in the switcher
